WEBVTT

00:00:30.625 --> 00:00:33.708
You slide your arm
through the sleeve, see?

00:00:33.708 --> 00:00:36.708
Next, you place the left side on top...

00:00:36.708 --> 00:00:39.292
and that's how you put it on. Understand?

00:00:39.292 --> 00:00:41.208
Like this...?

00:00:41.208 --> 00:00:43.125
<i>She's got plenty of merit, too. </i>

00:00:43.125 --> 00:00:45.333
<i>Is there still some room for growth?</i>

00:00:45.333 --> 00:00:47.917
Geez, what is the deal with these clothes?

00:00:47.917 --> 00:00:49.125
<i>And those...</i>

00:00:49.125 --> 00:00:52.708
<i>are one-of-a-kind specimens,</i>
<i>for those so inclined!</i>

00:00:52.708 --> 00:00:55.792
It's called a <i>yukata</i>.

00:00:55.792 --> 00:00:59.125
They're having a festival at
the local shrine today.

00:01:00.125 --> 00:01:01.958
Ah, Master...

00:01:04.500 --> 00:01:06.708
That was quite tasty.

00:01:08.333 --> 00:01:10.625
Tomo, you sicko!

00:01:11.042 --> 00:01:14.083
<i>I can hear my heart bell</i>

00:01:14.083 --> 00:01:16.667
<i>What could it mean?</i>

00:01:16.667 --> 00:01:20.375
<i>A bell in my heart is ringing</i>

00:01:21.833 --> 00:01:26.042
"Heaven's Lost Property"

00:01:26.167 --> 00:01:31.917
<i>It all started way back then </i>
<i>(ringin' ringin')</i>

00:01:31.917 --> 00:01:37.500
<i>Ever since before we were born</i>
<i>(ringin' ringin')</i>

00:01:37.500 --> 00:01:42.750
<i>you were destined to appear out of nowhere,</i>

00:01:42.750 --> 00:01:45.750
<i>right before my eyes,</i>

00:01:45.750 --> 00:01:48.542
<i>I'm sure of it</i>

00:01:48.542 --> 00:01:54.208
<i>My wishes and ambitions and daydreams</i>

00:01:54.208 --> 00:01:59.875
<i>take me to an unknown level and knock on a door</i>

00:01:59.875 --> 00:02:06.083
<i>You give me the key and the future</i>
<i>I need to take flight (with your wings)</i>

00:02:06.083 --> 00:02:09.000
<i>I can hear my heart bell</i>

00:02:09.000 --> 00:02:12.042
<i>There's no stopping it</i>

00:02:12.042 --> 00:02:17.708
<i>It's a sign, rung by an angel, saying "I love you"</i>

00:02:17.708 --> 00:02:20.583
<i>Can you hear my heart bell?</i>

00:02:20.583 --> 00:02:22.917
<i>What could it mean?</i>

00:02:22.917 --> 00:02:28.333
<i>A bell in my heart that I've </i>
<i>never heard before is ringing</i>

00:02:28.333 --> 00:02:37.458
<i>But even so, you don't suspect a thing</i>

00:02:42.292 --> 00:02:45.625
The Age of Exploration
began in the 15th century.

00:02:45.625 --> 00:02:49.750
One might also say that it
was a time of brutal colonization

00:02:49.750 --> 00:02:52.500
by the countries of Western Europe.

00:02:52.500 --> 00:02:55.042
Europeans, with guns in their right hands,

00:02:55.042 --> 00:02:57.292
and Bibles in their left,

00:02:57.292 --> 00:03:00.000
discovered New Worlds, one after another,

00:03:00.000 --> 00:03:02.583
and began invading them by force.

00:03:02.583 --> 00:03:05.750
The first musket that mankind took up

00:03:05.750 --> 00:03:09.875
was indeed a symbol
of conquest of the New World.

00:03:30.833 --> 00:03:33.458
A gun in his right hand...

00:03:34.958 --> 00:03:37.500
"For Whom the Shooting Festival is Held"

00:03:38.208 --> 00:03:41.625
Wow, it's in full swing again this year!

00:03:41.625 --> 00:03:43.125
The cotton candy looks delicious!

00:03:43.125 --> 00:03:45.792
I want some <i>takoyaki</i>
and <i>yakisoba</i>, too!

00:03:45.792 --> 00:03:47.583
That's all food, isn't it?

00:03:47.583 --> 00:03:49.250
So what? Who cares?

00:03:49.250 --> 00:03:51.583
If you eat too much of that, you'll get fat--

00:03:51.583 --> 00:03:54.875
N-Never mind, nothing!

00:04:00.292 --> 00:04:02.208
What, do you want one?

00:04:02.208 --> 00:04:04.042
Not really.

00:04:05.542 --> 00:04:09.583
Hey, Ikaros! If you want
anything, I'll buy it for you.

00:04:09.583 --> 00:04:11.583
Master, these...

00:04:13.375 --> 00:04:16.583
No! You can have just one!

00:04:16.583 --> 00:04:19.250
Tomo, aren't you going
to come look at the stands?

00:04:19.250 --> 00:04:21.542
I'll be right there!

00:04:23.333 --> 00:04:25.792
Hmm? What's this?

00:04:28.167 --> 00:04:30.417
What is all this?

00:04:36.917 --> 00:04:38.417
Welcome.

00:04:40.375 --> 00:04:44.667
Hey, Tomo, there's something
not right about this shooting gallery.

00:04:45.917 --> 00:04:47.708
There are nothing but guns in his shop,

00:04:47.708 --> 00:04:50.625
and I don't see a single prize anywhere.

00:04:51.583 --> 00:04:54.917
It's a shooting gallery, but it
doesn't have any targets to shoot at.

00:04:54.917 --> 00:04:56.833
Sugata, you're here?

00:04:56.833 --> 00:04:59.125
Yeah. Mikako called me out.

00:04:59.125 --> 00:05:02.417
What is a festival?

00:05:03.958 --> 00:05:05.875
Festivals were originally something

00:05:05.875 --> 00:05:09.042
where the whole town came
together to have fun, were they not?

00:05:09.042 --> 00:05:10.875
Chairman...

00:05:10.875 --> 00:05:13.625
And so, the Satsukitane Family,

00:05:13.625 --> 00:05:17.000
wanting the whole town to enjoy itself together,

00:05:17.000 --> 00:05:19.875
has called in a professional
night stand operator.

00:05:19.875 --> 00:05:22.042
I'm getting a bad feeling about this.

00:05:22.042 --> 00:05:23.750
The rules are simple.

00:05:23.750 --> 00:05:26.625
We're going to hold a
survival game with those cork guns,

00:05:26.625 --> 00:05:30.958
and the last one standing will
be presented with a fabulous prize.

00:05:30.958 --> 00:05:33.125
A fabulous prize?

00:05:33.125 --> 00:05:37.125
Yes, this. Ten million in cash!

00:05:39.667 --> 00:05:42.458
Indeed. That's enough to buy even dreams.

00:05:42.458 --> 00:05:44.000
Isn't that what you're saying?

00:05:44.000 --> 00:05:45.417
Whoa, Sugata!

00:05:45.417 --> 00:05:49.958
That sounds like it could be fun!
Let's play, too, Tomo!

00:05:51.208 --> 00:05:54.542
<i>Sure, the ten million is appealing,</i>

00:05:54.542 --> 00:05:58.500
<i>but I still have a bad feeling about this.</i>

00:06:05.167 --> 00:06:07.792
Nymph, aren't you going to participate?

00:06:07.792 --> 00:06:10.875
Nope. I'm not interested.

00:06:10.875 --> 00:06:13.625
Okay then, people of the town...

00:06:13.625 --> 00:06:17.917
...let's all have a great time
shooting each other up!

00:06:19.583 --> 00:06:22.625
Survival game start!

00:06:25.250 --> 00:06:27.375
<i>I can't afford to be hit by stray fire.</i>

00:06:27.375 --> 00:06:30.667
<i>I'll hide someplace for a little while.</i>

00:06:31.625 --> 00:06:34.083
Where do you think you're going, Tomo?!

00:06:34.083 --> 00:06:36.333
Th-The old lady from the community center!

00:06:36.333 --> 00:06:38.333
Are your feet no longer hurting you?

00:06:38.333 --> 00:06:43.750
For ten million, that pain has gone packing!

00:06:44.792 --> 00:06:47.917
Hold it, Tomo! Have you forgotten?

00:06:47.917 --> 00:06:50.917
You owe me for changing your diapers!

00:06:53.333 --> 00:06:55.708
Say your prayers, Tomo!

00:06:55.708 --> 00:06:56.917
The woman from the grocery!

00:06:56.917 --> 00:06:58.458
Hey, you, you're not getting away!

00:06:58.458 --> 00:07:01.167
The guy from the fish shop!

00:07:05.083 --> 00:07:06.667
I see Sakurai!

00:07:06.667 --> 00:07:11.500
The girls from class, too?!
Why is everyone out to get me?!

00:07:11.500 --> 00:07:14.542
You sure are loved, huh, Sakurai?

00:07:14.542 --> 00:07:17.625
I don't need this kind of love!

00:07:22.000 --> 00:07:23.708
Am I safe?

00:07:23.708 --> 00:07:25.167
You wish!

00:07:25.167 --> 00:07:26.792
Oh, no!

00:07:27.958 --> 00:07:30.542
You're all mine!

00:07:33.875 --> 00:07:35.375
G-Granny!

00:07:36.125 --> 00:07:37.542
Ow!

00:07:38.208 --> 00:07:39.958
S-Sniper!

00:07:39.958 --> 00:07:41.917
Where's it coming from?!

00:07:53.250 --> 00:07:54.667
Buddy!

00:08:01.917 --> 00:08:04.792
<i>Looks like there's another</i>
<i>sniper here besides me.</i>

00:08:04.792 --> 00:08:07.708
<i>The chilling way in which</i>
<i>they conceal their presence,</i>

00:08:07.708 --> 00:08:11.125
<i>as well as the incomparable</i>
<i>accuracy of their shot...</i>

00:08:11.125 --> 00:08:13.542
<i>There's no doubt about it.</i>

00:08:13.542 --> 00:08:15.625
<i>Mikako, it's you.</i>

00:08:32.750 --> 00:08:34.167
Not bad, Mikako.

00:08:34.167 --> 00:08:36.875
You, too, Ei.

00:08:36.875 --> 00:08:39.542
Stop it! Help me!

00:08:40.750 --> 00:08:42.333
I'd say we're evenly matched!

00:08:42.333 --> 00:08:45.167
Then let's settle it with these!

00:08:47.875 --> 00:08:50.042
If I'd known this would happen,
I would have let myself be done in

00:08:50.042 --> 00:08:53.583
by the guys from the shopping district!

00:08:53.583 --> 00:08:56.292
Help! We're gonna get killed!

00:09:02.083 --> 00:09:03.500
<i>What...</i>

00:09:05.042 --> 00:09:06.542
<i>...is that?</i>

00:09:19.208 --> 00:09:21.542
It's the end of the world!

00:09:21.542 --> 00:09:26.667
God has come to destroy us!

00:09:29.917 --> 00:09:33.125
Hey! You're overdoing it!

00:09:33.125 --> 00:09:35.583
You've done enough! Behave yourself now!

00:09:35.583 --> 00:09:37.833
Yes, Master.

00:09:37.833 --> 00:09:41.917
Then again, thanks to Ikaros,
there are a lot fewer people now.

00:09:41.917 --> 00:09:46.583
Does this mean I actually
have a shot at that ten million?

00:09:46.583 --> 00:09:48.875
All right, let's go!

00:10:02.292 --> 00:10:06.417
How did it feel to lay
waste to the ground like that?

00:10:06.417 --> 00:10:08.708
Did it take you back?

00:10:08.708 --> 00:10:14.708
What's the use? Your memories
and thoughts have been blocked.

00:10:15.875 --> 00:10:18.792
In that case, allow me to help you remember...

00:10:18.792 --> 00:10:22.917
...your true form: the one
feared as the Uranus Queen,

00:10:22.917 --> 00:10:26.208
that rocked all of Synapse!

00:10:28.250 --> 00:10:33.292
Well? Remember
anything yet, Uranus Queen?

00:10:33.292 --> 00:10:37.375
I am a pet-type Angeloid,

00:10:37.375 --> 00:10:39.167
type Alpha...

00:10:39.167 --> 00:10:42.542
Pet-type? Don't make me laugh.

00:10:42.542 --> 00:10:46.708
I was told by my master
to bring you back to Synapse.

00:10:47.708 --> 00:10:52.667
Something that is misplaced should
be taken back to its owner, Alpha.

00:10:59.167 --> 00:11:02.125
I told you to be careful.

00:11:02.875 --> 00:11:07.167
"Heaven's Lost Property"

00:11:14.833 --> 00:11:18.625
I am an electronic warfare-type
Angeloid, type Beta, Nymph.

00:11:18.625 --> 00:11:21.875
I have come to get you, Uranus Queen.

00:11:22.792 --> 00:11:25.833
I am a pet-type...

00:11:25.833 --> 00:11:29.750
Are you still saying that?
You don't know when to quit!

00:11:30.625 --> 00:11:34.042
Perhaps I'm punishing you too hard.

00:11:36.375 --> 00:11:39.042
I am...

00:11:39.042 --> 00:11:41.875
...a pet-type Angeloid...

00:11:44.125 --> 00:11:49.750
Fine. I'll use my hacking system
to remove your memory block.

00:11:49.750 --> 00:11:56.042
And then, you will remember that
you are not some two-bit pet-type!

00:12:02.375 --> 00:12:05.167
<i>What...? Something is coming to the surface...</i>

00:12:05.167 --> 00:12:06.750
Ikaros...

00:12:06.750 --> 00:12:11.833
...go and crush the Downers on the
Earth. Every last one of them.

00:12:11.833 --> 00:12:13.458
Yes, Master.

00:12:14.417 --> 00:12:17.000
<i>What is this memory...?</i>

00:12:33.333 --> 00:12:35.292
<i>Stop!</i>

00:12:35.292 --> 00:12:37.667
I'm sorry I got upset at you last night.

00:12:37.667 --> 00:12:40.958
You were acting like one
of those humanoid weapons,

00:12:40.958 --> 00:12:43.375
like you see in the movies.

00:12:43.375 --> 00:12:48.458
I was just thinking, that's sort
of something I wouldn't like.

00:12:49.667 --> 00:12:51.167
<i>Master...</i>

00:13:06.583 --> 00:13:09.333
What, it hurts so much,
it brought you to tears?

00:13:09.333 --> 00:13:12.625
Finding out that you're not a pet-type?

00:13:16.125 --> 00:13:21.500
Hey, just a minute. Why are you able to cry?

00:13:21.500 --> 00:13:24.375
All I removed was
the block on your memory.

00:13:24.375 --> 00:13:27.083
I didn't remove the block on your thoughts!

00:13:32.750 --> 00:13:36.000
Emotional block 100% removed.

00:13:36.000 --> 00:13:38.958
Variable wing block removal in progress.

00:13:38.958 --> 00:13:41.542
--80%... 90%...
--It can't be!

00:13:41.542 --> 00:13:44.000
Initiating self-repair program.

00:13:44.000 --> 00:13:47.500
Function block removal
in progress. 80%... 90%...

00:13:47.500 --> 00:13:50.958
Are you reawakening completely,
Uranus Queen?

00:13:53.958 --> 00:13:56.125
Self-repair complete.

00:13:56.125 --> 00:13:59.292
Target lock on.

00:13:59.292 --> 00:14:01.333
Artemis firing.

00:14:09.417 --> 00:14:14.417
<i>How?! How did she remove all</i>
<i>of her blocks?! She has awakened!</i>

00:14:20.125 --> 00:14:21.750
Oh, no!

00:14:32.167 --> 00:14:35.500
Mud! There's mud on my face!

00:14:35.500 --> 00:14:37.292
No!!

00:14:37.292 --> 00:14:39.667
No! No! I'm dirty! I'm dirty! I'm dirty!

00:14:39.667 --> 00:14:42.125
I hate anything dirty!

00:14:42.125 --> 00:14:45.583
Why, you! I'll smash you to pieces!

00:14:45.583 --> 00:14:47.583
Paradise Song!!

00:14:54.208 --> 00:14:56.208
Ae-Aegis!

00:15:03.542 --> 00:15:05.042
That arrow...

00:15:05.042 --> 00:15:06.667
Apollon!

00:15:08.042 --> 00:15:11.625
Are you crazy?! Are you trying
to blow the whole country away?!

00:15:11.625 --> 00:15:14.875
It is all right. Once it strikes you,

00:15:14.875 --> 00:15:18.333
I will extend the defensive field
Aegis to full, protecting the land.

00:15:18.333 --> 00:15:19.417
That's absurd!

00:15:19.417 --> 00:15:22.625
If you do that, you're not going
to come away unscathed, either!

00:15:22.625 --> 00:15:26.125
I will go back to my master.

00:15:26.125 --> 00:15:31.792
I am a pet-type Angeloid, type Alpha, Ikaros.

00:15:31.792 --> 00:15:36.083
Please... stand down... Nymph...

00:15:43.458 --> 00:15:46.833
Please...

00:15:46.833 --> 00:15:48.833
All right.

00:15:50.083 --> 00:15:54.500
But how long can you go on fooling him?

00:15:54.500 --> 00:15:56.375
I wonder what your master will think

00:15:56.375 --> 00:15:59.417
once he finds out what you really are,

00:15:59.417 --> 00:16:03.125
you weapon of mass destruction!

00:16:12.125 --> 00:16:17.167
And here, Master
told me to behave myself...

00:16:17.167 --> 00:16:18.792
Master...

00:16:21.083 --> 00:16:28.458
Say, mister, how many more
people are left? I'm exhausted.

00:16:28.458 --> 00:16:31.458
Hey, mister, are you listening?

00:16:39.458 --> 00:16:42.958
Mister... does--does that mean...?

00:16:42.958 --> 00:16:47.583
Yeah, a real gun got mixed in.

00:16:47.583 --> 00:16:50.792
I wouldn't be surprised if there
was another one mixed in, as well.

00:16:50.792 --> 00:16:53.250
Tomo, I found you!

00:16:54.167 --> 00:16:56.625
I've been looking for you for a long time.

00:16:56.625 --> 00:17:01.250
But Tomo, you weren't anywhere
to be found. Being left all alone...

00:17:01.250 --> 00:17:02.875
...isn't any fun!

00:17:02.875 --> 00:17:05.667
M-Mister, that's not the one, right?

00:17:05.667 --> 00:17:08.458
--Tomo, say your prayers!
--Yeah, that's it...

00:17:09.708 --> 00:17:11.875
Wow, incredible!

00:17:11.875 --> 00:17:15.750
The toys they have these days
are really well made, huh?

00:17:15.750 --> 00:17:18.458
Sohara, wait! Take it easy!

00:17:18.458 --> 00:17:19.750
How fun!

00:17:19.750 --> 00:17:22.875
It's funny, right? There's something
funny about that gun, right?

00:17:22.875 --> 00:17:28.000
I want to win this game, no matter what!
If I win, I get ten million!

00:17:28.000 --> 00:17:29.625
Stop!!

00:17:29.625 --> 00:17:34.542
<i>If I get that ten million,</i>
<i>I can do all sorts of things.</i>

00:17:34.542 --> 00:17:37.375
<i>I can go to the amusement park with Tomo...</i>

00:17:37.375 --> 00:17:40.000
<i>I can go on trips with Tomo...</i>

00:17:40.000 --> 00:17:41.917
<i>and when we get to where we're staying...</i>

00:17:41.917 --> 00:17:46.667
<i>Tomo, you sicko,</i>
<i>you want to join me for a bath...?</i>

00:17:50.833 --> 00:17:54.333
Oh, Tomo, you sicko!
What are you thinking, you idiot?!

00:17:54.333 --> 00:17:57.583
I'm begging you, take it easy!

00:17:57.583 --> 00:17:59.417
S-Stop! Stop!

00:17:59.417 --> 00:18:05.333
Tomo, if there's no one else
left, then I win, you know.

00:18:05.333 --> 00:18:07.583
You want to win that badly?

00:18:07.583 --> 00:18:10.292
What are you going
to do with the ten million?!

00:18:10.292 --> 00:18:14.500
Well, I... Well, I...

00:18:14.500 --> 00:18:18.708
No, I can't! It's so embarrassing,
I can't say it!

00:18:18.708 --> 00:18:20.708
Tomo, you sicko!

00:18:23.000 --> 00:18:25.042
Somebody, help!

00:18:42.375 --> 00:18:45.000
You're... kidding, right?

00:18:49.500 --> 00:18:53.750
Ikaros!!

00:18:53.750 --> 00:18:55.167
Yes?

00:18:57.958 --> 00:19:03.167
Sheesh, what kind of body have you got?
You really had me worried.

00:19:10.667 --> 00:19:12.667
Come to think of it, where is Nymph?

00:19:12.667 --> 00:19:18.667
Knowing her, she probably got
tired of waiting, and went on home.

00:19:18.667 --> 00:19:22.042
Incidentally, just who exactly is the victor?

00:19:22.042 --> 00:19:23.917
That's right, the ten million!

00:19:23.917 --> 00:19:28.500
It looked to me like it was
down to just Tomoki and Mitsuki.

00:19:28.500 --> 00:19:29.750
Are you serious?!

00:19:29.750 --> 00:19:32.042
No, there's still him.

00:19:42.125 --> 00:19:45.583
Make this good, mama's boy.

00:20:21.167 --> 00:20:25.833
The winner is the man from the night stand!

00:20:27.042 --> 00:20:29.417
Here. Your half.

00:20:29.417 --> 00:20:30.833
Yeah.

00:20:36.667 --> 00:20:39.458
I'll see you again next year!

00:20:39.458 --> 00:20:43.083
He's coming back next year?!

00:20:44.000 --> 00:20:46.167
"1st Sorami"
"Survival Game"

00:20:47.167 --> 00:20:49.542
"The seven warriors
who fell on the battlefield"

00:20:53.167 --> 00:20:55.167
<i> </i>
<i>If there's something that you can't do,</i>

00:20:55.167 --> 00:20:57.208
"The Grocer Lady"
<i>If there's something that you can't do,</i>

00:20:59.292 --> 00:21:04.958
<i>I will do it myself</i>

00:21:04.958 --> 00:21:05.375
"The Fish Market Guy"

00:21:05.375 --> 00:21:07.125
"The Fish Market Guy"
<i>Yeah,</i>

